    "measurementTechnique": [
      "For a full description of the process of development of this reporting format, refer to Ely KS et al (in review). A reporting format for leaf-level gas exchange data and metadata. Ecological Informatics.\nFor the latest update on the reporting format, please access the documentation on GitHub or GitBook.\nhttps://github.com/ess-dive-community/essdive-leaf-gas-exchange\nhttps://ess-dive.gitbook.io/leaf-level-gas-exchange/",
      "To reach community consensus on the content of this reporting format, subject matter experts from many organizations were invited to participate, including from the following ESS projects:\nAmeriflux\nCarbon Dynamics within Urban-Suburban-Forested-Agricultural Landscapes\nClimate Change Feedbacks from Interactions Between New and Old Carbon;\nClimate change impacts at the temperate-boreal ecotone: interactions between warming and precipitation;\nConnecting AmeriFlux to the Globe, Extending the Partnership with Global Flux Network FLUXNET;\nConstraining the Simultaneous Effects of Elevated CO2, Temperature, and Shifts in Rainfall Patterns on Ecosystem Carbon Fluxes using Multi-Scale Resource;\nDetermining the impact of forest mortality in semi-arid woodlands on local and regional carbon dynamics;\nEffects of Hurricane Disturbance and Increased Temperature on Carbon Cycling and Storage of a Puerto Rican Forest: A Mechanistic Investigation of Above- and Belowground Processes;\nNext Generation Ecosystem Experiments - Arctic;\nNext Generation Ecosystem Experiments - Tropics;\nORNL Terrestrial Ecosystem Science Scientific Focus Area;\nPartitioning CO2 Fluxes with Isotopologue Measurements and Modeling to Understand Mechanisms of Forest Carbon Sequestration;\nQuantifying the Effect of Nighttime Interactions Between Roots and Canopy Physiology and Their Control of Water and Carbon Cycling on Feedbacks Between Soil Moisture and Terrestrial Climatology under Variable Environmental Conditions;\nSpruce and Peatland Responses Under Changing Environments;\nSubalpine and Alpine Species Range Shifts with Climate Change: Temperature and Soil Moisture Manipulations to Test Species and Population Response;\nUnderstanding the Response of Photosynthetic Metabolism in Tropical Forests to Seasonal Climate Variation"
    ],
